<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seuthopolis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 320 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seuthopolis was the capital founded around 320 BCE by the Odrysian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seuthes-iii">Seuthes III</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazanlak">Kazanlak</a> valley of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. Laid out on a regular Greek plan with a fortified royal residence and sanctuary, it was excavated in 1948–1954 before being flooded by the Koprinka <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reservoir">Reservoir</a>. It is one of the few Thracian cities known in detail.</p></div>
